{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Wire the copilot, codex, and claude client configs to connect to the rebar MCP endpoint over remote\nHTTP with a `static` bearer PAT (ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur; PATs from exuberant-blockish-avians).\nSingle concern: the three client-side config shapes + a basic read-tool smoke — the endpoint/edge is\nesok, the credentials are avians, live prod verification is jackal.\n\n## Approach + rationale (research-confirmed static bearer for all three)\nResearch confirmed all three clients support a static `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header for a\nremote HTTP MCP server and none require OAuth, so one auth shape covers all three:\n- **Copilot**: `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json` — the rebar server entry with the HTTPS `/mcp/` URL and a\n  `headers` map carrying `Authorization: Bearer <PAT>`.\n- **Codex**: `~/.codex/config.toml` — TOML server entry using `bearer_token_env_var` (or\n  `http_headers`/`env_http_headers`) so the PAT comes from the environment, not the committed file.\n- **Claude**: `.mcp.json` (`headers`) or `--header`. Document the gotcha: a static header takes\n  precedence and does NOT fall back to OAuth if rejected, so a wrong/expired PAT fails hard (not a\n  silent OAuth retry).\nEach references the gitignored credential from avians (env var / local file), never an inline secret.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (in-session)\n- Tier: **real client config load + a basic read-tool call** (test-design §3 \"external-service\n  mapping\" via a reachable staging endpoint or a local `rebar-mcp` HTTP instance). Oracles:\n  - Each of the three configs is accepted by its client and lists the `rebar` MCP server (assert via\n    each client's server-list command), against a reachable endpoint.\n  - Each client executes ONE basic read tool (e.g. a ticket `show`/`list`) successfully through the\n    HTTP transport with the bearer header (oracle: a real tool result, not just \"connected\").\n  - Contrast (§6): an absent/invalid bearer yields an auth failure surfaced to the client (401), not\n    a hang — confirming the header is actually on the request path.\n- No secret is committed (the PAT is sourced from the avians env var / gitignored file).\n\n## Compat / rollback\nAdditive client config; rollback = remove the three server entries. No server-side change.\n\nDepends on: cibophobic-holohedral-esok (reachable endpoint), exuberant-blockish-avians (PATs).\nBlocks: creased-childlike-jackal (live prod verification)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787598340298510001,"uuid":"52683c1e-2615-48d3-b04a-2f03e26d301e"}